From: H713 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] h713: build the host tools without OpenSSL

The H713 boards do not sign images: the FIT the build packages is
unsigned and U-Boot does not verify signatures at boot. Even so, the
default host-tool configuration links mkimage against OpenSSL's
libcrypto (TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO, also selected by TOOLS_KWBIMAGE for Marvell
images). OpenSSL 4 removed the ENGINE API that lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c uses,
so on an up-to-date host the tools no longer link and the whole U-Boot
build fails.

Turn both host-tool options off for the two H713 boards. They affect
host tools only ("does not affect target features"); the target SPL and
proper are byte-identical with and without them. The build then no
longer depends on the host's OpenSSL at all.

--- a/configs/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
+++ b/configs/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
@@ -61,3 +61,5 @@
 CONFIG_H713_VENDOR_CHAINLOAD=y
 CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
+# CONFIG_TOOLS_KWBIMAGE is not set
+# CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
--- a/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig
@@ -53,3 +53,5 @@
 CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
 CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x400000
 CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
+# CONFIG_TOOLS_KWBIMAGE is not set
+# CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
